{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DESIGN DECISIONS (settled with maintainer @JoeOakhartNava). Landing order: bb9b lands AFTER 0347 (0347 shrinks how often a coverage-gap -1 is cast; bb9b is the manual escape hatch for the residual + the bounded-retry escalation).\n\nMechanism: a MANUAL escape hatch (not an automated retrier). Reuse the existing forced-re-review machinery (app.py POST /rerun -> _rebar_force -> voter.review_and_vote bypassing dedup/existing-vote, which overwrites the LLM-Review label -> satisfies \"replace the stale -1\"). Add a server-side ELIGIBILITY PRECHECK in front of it.\n\nEligibility discriminator (works from current messaging — no separate state store): read the bot`s current-revision LLM-Review -1 vote MESSAGE TAG back from Gerrit`s authoritative vote record. Only bots/admins can cast LLM-Review, so a contributor cannot forge the tag -> this is privileged-side durable state, NOT the contributor`s claim. Needs a small gerrit_client method to fetch the latest LLM-Review vote value+message tag on the current revision.\n\nPer-sub-reason eligibility for the MANUAL trigger:\n* ELIGIBLE: llm-unavailable, review-error, scanner, indeterminate.\n* REFUSED (with a message saying why): finding (the security property of this feature) and gate-disabled (a config state that yields the identical result forever).\n\nNo artificial numeric retry cap: it is manual by construction (a human acts each time), so it cannot spam a loop; the eligibility gate (refusing finding/gate-disabled) IS the bound, and it is observable via the refusal message + logs.\n\nSecurity AC tests: (1) a contributor CANNOT clear a real BLOCK finding by re-triggering; (2) eligibility cannot be obtained via any contributor-controlled input; (3) no path lets a contributor cause an LLM-Review +1 without the review actually running and passing.\n\nSTILL OPEN (settle when we start bb9b): the contributor-facing surface — a token-gated HTTP endpoint is not contributor-reachable, so likely a magic Gerrit comment (add comment-added to the review-bot webhooks.config) funnelling into the same precheck; keyword TBD (proposed `re-review`, since `recheck` is taken by CI/g2p).\n\nAlso update CONTRIBUTING.md 2c and docs/review-policy.md: the \"a maintainer re-triggers it\" instruction becomes the contributor-accessible path, finding still requires a real fix."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785692406209198001,"uuid":"5e6943e4-6524-4a30-a12f-3b73c8d24757"}